/*
====================================================================
 PRO FIX v7.5 - ULTIMATE HYBRID FIRMWARE (UNAVAILABLE-SCREEN PROMPT)
 ESP32 + SIM800L (.AMR audio) + 9 RELAYS + MULTI-SMS + WATCHDOG
 Integrated Features:
  - Non-blocking Unified UART Parser & Async Watchdog
  - Postponed SMS during active call/pulses (No PC hard-off)
  - Pin 13 instead of 14 for Relay 6 (Boot glitch fixed)
  - Under-voltage & Power-down detection
  - SMS '>' prompt wait with ESC cancel
  - Audio playback via AT+CMEDPLAY + AT+CRSL/AT+CLVL (confirmed working)
  - Up to three screen/PC groups (A/B/C) — 9 relays total
  - SMS text sent in Russian (Cyrillic), UCS2 + correct DCS
  - DEVICE_ADDRESS text prepended to every phase-status SMS
  - SCREEN_COUNT compile-time switch to enable 1, 2, or 3 groups
  - Voice feedback ("недоступно") when pressing a screen digit that
    SCREEN_COUNT doesn't have configured

 CHANGES vs v7.4:
  - ADDED: a 6th voice prompt file is now needed on the modem's
    filesystem — "C:\User\0006.amr". Record something like "Экран
    недоступен, выберите другой пункт" or "Неверный выбор". Upload it
    the same way you uploaded 0001-0005.amr.
  - CHANGED: pressing "2" from the root menu when SCREEN_COUNT < 2, or
    "3" when SCREEN_COUNT < 3, now plays 0006.amr instead of doing
    nothing. The caller stays in ROOT_MENU (menu state is NOT changed,
    unlike a real selection) so they can immediately try a valid
    digit again without having to press "0" first.
  - This matters specifically because 0001.amr (the root-menu prompt)
    is a static recording — it doesn't know SCREEN_COUNT and will
    keep saying "нажмите три" even when group C isn't wired up. This
    change means pressing 3 on such a device at least gets an
    audible "not available" response instead of silence, rather than
    requiring you to re-record 0001.amr per site to match its actual
    SCREEN_COUNT.

 CHANGES vs v7.3 (carried over from v7.4):
  - ADDED: utf8ToUcs2Hex() — converts a UTF-8 String (as stored in
    this .ino file, which Arduino IDE saves as UTF-8 by default) into
    the HEX-encoded UCS2 (UTF-16BE) format SIM800 requires for
    non-Latin SMS text.
  - CHANGED: sendSMS() now switches the modem to AT+CSCS="UCS2" right
    before sending (encoding both the phone number and the message
    body as UCS2 hex), then switches back to AT+CSCS="GSM" (plain
    ASCII) immediately after. The switch-back is important: leaving
    UCS2 on globally would break AT+CMEDPLAY's plain-ASCII file path
    argument used by playAmr().
  - CHANGED: all SMS body text (boot message, phase status, denied
    call notification) translated to Russian.
  - NOTE: this firmware's own .ino source must stay saved as UTF-8
    (Arduino IDE's default) for the Cyrillic literals in the code to
    convert correctly — if you ever re-save it with a different
    encoding, the Russian text will come out corrupted.

 CHANGES vs v6.9 (carried over from v7.0):
  - ADDED: Relay 7 (Screen C power, 220V) on GPIO14
  - ADDED: Relay 8 (PC C power SW) on GPIO18
  - ADDED: Relay 9 (PC C reset SW) on GPIO19
    GPIO14/18/19 chosen because they are free on this board's pinout
    (not already used by SIM800/phases/relays 1-6) and are NOT ESP32
    strapping pins (0, 2, 12, 15), so they're safe as plain outputs.
  - ADDED: MENU_C DTMF menu — press "3" from the root menu (in
    addition to existing "1"=Screen/PC A, "2"=Screen/PC B) to reach
    the same 1/2/3/0 sub-menu for group C.
  - ADDED: a 5th voice prompt file is now needed on the modem's
    filesystem — "C:\User\0005.amr" — played when entering MENU_C
    (analogous to 0002.amr for menu A, 0003.amr for menu B). Record
    and upload it the same way you uploaded 0001-0004.amr, or DTMF
    "3" will trigger playback of a file that doesn't exist and the
    modem will likely just respond ERROR/silently fail — the relay
    logic itself does not depend on this file being present.
  - Output arrays (outputPins/pinState/pinTimer/pinDuration) and all
    loops over them (anyOutputBusy, outputHandler) extended from 6 to
    9 elements — this was necessary and is a mechanical, not logical,
    change: any hardcoded "6" would have silently ignored relays 7-9.
====================================================================
*/

